        ('9004001f-0000-4000-8000-00000000000e', 'Q14. You recently visited an old age home with your school voluntary service club. Write a Descriptive Paragraph in about 100-120 words describing your observations, the residents'' emotions, and the impact the visit left on your mind.', NULL, NULL, 'LA', 'English', 'Descriptive Paragraph', 5, 'A Visit to the Old Age Home: Last Saturday, our school voluntary club visited ''Sandhya Aashray'', a serene refuge for senior citizens. Walking into the sunny courtyard, we were greeted by silver-haired elders whose eyes reflected both wisdom and an unspoken yearning for companionship. We spent the afternoon singing melodious vintage songs, reciting poetry, and listening to their poignant life journeys. Mrs. Shanti, an eighty-year-old retired teacher, affectionately held my hand while reminiscing about her teaching days. Despite physical frailties, their grace and warm smiles were deeply touching. However, a lingering melancholy pervaded the corridors, revealing the quiet sting of abandonment by their busy families. The experience awakened in me a profound sense of gratitude and reaffirmed that our elders deserve dignity, unconditional love, and constant care.', '2 Marks for content relevance and vivid sensory descriptions; 2 Marks for organization and vocabulary; 1 Mark for grammatical accuracy', NULL, NULL, 'MEDIUM', true),
        ('9004001f-0000-4000-8000-00000000000f', 'Q15. Reference to Context (Poetry - The Road Not Taken): ''Two roads diverged in a yellow wood, / And sorry I could not travel both / And be one traveler, long I stood / And looked down one as far as I could...'' (i) What do the ''two diverging roads'' symbolize in human life? (ii) Why did the poet choose the second road? (iii) What does the phrase ''yellow wood'' signify?', NULL, NULL, 'CASE', 'English', 'The Road Not Taken', 5, '(i) The two diverging roads symbolize the inevitable, fateful choices and decisions that every individual must make in the journey of life. (ii) The poet chose the second road because it was grassy, less traveled by the crowd, and ''wanted wear'', representing an unconventional, bold path. (iii) ''Yellow wood'' signifies the autumn season, representing maturity, change, and the passage of time.', '1.5 Marks for symbolical interpretation of roads; 2 Marks for justifying road choice; 1.5 Marks for autumn season significance', NULL, NULL, 'MEDIUM', true),
