        ('90040032-0000-4000-8000-00000000000b', 'Q11. Reported Speech: Rahul said, ''I have finished my science experiment.'' The indirect speech is:', '{"A":"Rahul said that he had finished his science experiment.","B":"Rahul said that he has finished his science experiment.","C":"Rahul told that he finished his science experiment.","D":"Rahul says he has finished his science experiment."}'::jsonb, 'A', 'MCQ', 'English', 'Reported Speech', 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Present perfect (''have finished'') shifts to past perfect (''had finished'') in indirect speech when reporting verb is in the past.', 'MEDIUM', true),
        ('90040032-0000-4000-8000-00000000000c', 'Q12. Fill in the blank with the correct tense: ''By the time the rescue team arrived, the local villagers _______ the injured passengers.''', '{"A":"evacuated","B":"had evacuated","C":"have evacuated","D":"are evacuating"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'MCQ', 'English', 'Tenses', 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'The past perfect tense (''had evacuated'') denotes the earlier completed action before another past event occurred.', 'MEDIUM', true),
        ('90040032-0000-4000-8000-00000000000d', 'Q13. You recently visited an old age home with your school voluntary service club. Write a Descriptive Paragraph in about 100-120 words describing your observations, the residents'' emotions, and the impact the visit left on your mind.', NULL, NULL, 'LA', 'English', 'Descriptive Paragraph', 5, 'A Visit to the Old Age Home: Last Saturday, our school voluntary club visited ''Sandhya Aashray'', a serene refuge for senior citizens. Walking into the sunny courtyard, we were greeted by silver-haired elders whose eyes reflected both wisdom and an unspoken yearning for companionship. We spent the afternoon singing melodious vintage songs, reciting poetry, and listening to their poignant life journeys. Mrs. Shanti, an eighty-year-old retired teacher, affectionately held my hand while reminiscing about her teaching days. Despite physical frailties, their grace and warm smiles were deeply touching. However, a lingering melancholy pervaded the corridors, revealing the quiet sting of abandonment by their busy families. The experience awakened in me a profound sense of gratitude and reaffirmed that our elders deserve dignity, unconditional love, and constant care.', '2 Marks for content relevance and vivid sensory descriptions; 2 Marks for organization and vocabulary; 1 Mark for grammatical accuracy', NULL, NULL, 'MEDIUM', true),
        ('90040032-0000-4000-8000-00000000000e', 'Q14. Taking inspiration from the theme of empathy and resilience, write a Diary Entry in about 100-120 words expressing your feelings when you helped a stray injured puppy recover and found it a loving home.', NULL, NULL, 'LA', 'English', 'Diary Entry', 5, 'Dear Diary,
